    "latest_update": "R-162 proves a nonzero neighbourhood for one actual shifted-state recursion rather than another one-shot coordinate. For any finite acyclic single pure-dyadic deterministic-matrix chain, the strict-lower-shift resolvent and its first three coefficient derivatives have constants independent of chain length. The new two-step origin acceleration has only the registered p-to-4p support and its full-action first-variation pairing vanishes at the centered stationary exact-torus origin, transferring the R-160 4/25 gap. Exact A1 dyadic synthesis gives c_Z^2<1; Q-Q0 is formed before norms and K0=0. A complete source/current/trace/projected-force/sextic modulus, including the mandatory 768M1c_Z term, yields delta_*=min(1/2,3/[100(1+L_*)]) and retains 13/100 as well as more than 1/10 of the induced recursive Gram. Arbitrary forests, random/nonlinear or revisit laws, pathwise conditional production Hessians, removal, and T-050 remain open.",
